# Simple Logical Proof - Resolution Steps
# Domain: Parent-Ancestor relationships
# File: examples/example.cnf

# Step 1: Resolve Parent(alice,bob) with ~Parent(X,Y) | Ancestor(X,Y)
# Clause [3]: Parent(alice, bob)
# Clause [1]: ~Parent(X, Y) | Ancestor(X, Y)
# Literals: [0] and [0]
# Unification: {X -> alice, Y -> bob}
# Resolvent: Ancestor(alice, bob)
3 0 1 0

# Step 2: Resolve Ancestor(alice,bob) with ~Ancestor(alice,bob)
# Clause [5]: Ancestor(alice, bob) (result from step 1)
# Clause [4]: ~Ancestor(alice, bob)
# Literals: [0] and [0]
# Unification: {} (empty)
# Resolvent: <empty clause> (NIL)
# Result: CONTRADICTION DERIVED -> Goal Ancestor(alice, bob) PROVED
5 0 4 0
